## Structure
- Feature-first: `lib/features/<feature>/{data,domain,ui}`; shared code in `lib/core`, app shell in `lib/app`.
- Tests mirror `lib/` under `test/`.
- Work inside the feature folder named in the task. Don't touch other features unless the task says so.

## Rules
- UI never calls the backend directly — go through a repository.
- No hard-coded colors, sizes or strings: use theme tokens and ARB localization.
- Never put secrets or paid API keys in the app. Use `--dart-define` only for public config.
- Ads: only through `AdsService`; dev flavor uses Google test ad unit IDs — never real ad IDs in dev or tests.
- Don't add a new package without stating why in the summary.
- Don't modify generated files (`*.g.dart`, `*.freezed.dart`); run build_runner instead.

## Commands
- Get deps: `flutter pub get`
- Codegen: `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs`
- Check: `flutter analyze` then `flutter test`
- Run dev: `flutter run --flavor dev -t lib/main_dev.dart`
- Release bundle: `flutter build appbundle --flavor prod -t lib/main_prod.dart --obfuscate --split-debug-info=build/symbols`

## Definition of done (every task)
1. Acceptance criteria in the task are met.
2. New logic has unit tests; new screens have at least one widget test.
3. `flutter analyze` has zero issues and `flutter test` passes.
4. Update `docs/TASKS.md` status for this task.
5. Reply with a summary of max 5 lines: what changed, files touched, anything risky or left undone.

## Token discipline
- Read only files needed for the task. Prefer searching over reading whole directories.
- When showing errors, include only the relevant lines.
- Keep replies short; no restating the task.
